{
  "_doc": [
    "The weights of the Mega-Dungeon template pools (read by tools/labyrinth/gen_mega_pools.py; docs/labyrinth/mega_arch.md explains every number).",
    "A pool is built from folders of structure/mega/<folder>/*.nbt. For a pool with `folders` (a map folder -> share) a template's weight is",
    "  share * scale * relative / (sum of the relative weights of that folder's templates), rounded, at least 1,",
    "so the SHARE of a folder in the pool stays what it is written here however many templates the folder holds (a builder adding ten halls does not",
    "drown the corridors). `relative` maps a template-id prefix (longest prefix wins, default 1) to its weight inside its folder.",
    "A pool with `absolute: true` uses `relative` as plain weights (default 1) instead. `filter` keeps only templates whose file name starts with it,",
    "`empty` adds an empty pool element of that weight (the assembler then draws the fallback pool: a door cap), `fallback` is the pool drawn after the",
    "elements. Vanilla limits a weight to 1..150."
  ],
  "scale": 20,
